        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Linen sampler embroidered with silk; English; mid 17th century."@en , "Linen embroidered with red and blue silk in alternating bands, showing patterns of various flowers and the alphabet."@en , "In their earliest form, samplers were put together as personal reference works for embroiderers. They were trials of patterns and stitches that had been copied from others, and records of particular effects achieved that could be recreated again. This is a type known as a band sampler. With the composition of band samplers comes the first clear indication in England of the form being used as a method of instruction and practice for girls learning needlework."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/c1525b8e-084a-39e6-a717-3d6e6714046b> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/2b2136c9-7fb9-3374-b8ee-ceee15534cd0> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "In their earliest form, samplers were put together as personal reference works for embroiderers. They were trials of patterns and stitches that had been copied from others, and records of particular effects achieved that could be recreated again. This is a type known as a band sampler. With the composition of band samplers comes the first clear indication in England of the form being used as a method of instruction and practice for girls learning needlework."@en , "Linen embroidered with red and blue silk in alternating bands, showing patterns of various flowers and the alphabet."@en , "Linen sampler embroidered with silk; English; mid 17th century."@en ;
